The models are still overfitting. XGBoost got 95.8% training accuracy but only 49.9% test accuracy. Let me fix the LightGBM error and try a different approach with more regularization and feature engineering.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/onehot_gradient_boosting.py",
    "old_str": "lgb_model.fit(X_train_oh, y_train,\n              eval_set=[(X_val_oh, y_val)],\n              eval_metric='binary_logloss',\n              verbose=False)",
    "new_str": "lgb_model.fit(X_train_oh, y_train,\n              eval_set=[(X_val_oh, y_val)],\n              eval_metric='binary_logloss',\n              callbacks=[lgb.log_evaluation(0)])"
  }
}
```

