The issue is that no rules passed the threshold (train_acc > 0.55 or train_acc < 0.45). This means even simple rules don't perform better than 55% on training data. Let me adjust the thresholds and debug.

```json
{
  "tool": "edit_file",
  "args": {
    "path": "code/rule_synthesis.py",
    "old_str": "                # Keep rules with reasonable performance\n                if train_acc > 0.55 or train_acc < 0.45:\n                    rules.append(rule)\n                    rule_descriptions.append(f\"Count({attribute}={target}) {comparison} {threshold}\")",
    "new_str": "                # Keep rules with reasonable performance\n                # Lower threshold since even weak signals might be useful\n                if train_acc > 0.53 or train_acc < 0.47:\n                    rules.append(rule)\n                    rule_descriptions.append(f\"Count({attribute}={target}) {comparison} {threshold}\")"
  }
}
```

